@startuml class-core
title Core types and the extraction contract

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package proc_macro_flow_traits <<Frame>> {

  class "Extraction<T>" as Extraction {
    +value: Option<T>
    +reasons: Vec<Reason>
    --
    +value(T) -> Self
    +failed(Reason) -> Self
    +with_reason(Reason) -> Self
    +is_failure() -> bool
    +absorb<U>(Extraction<U>) -> Option<U>
  }
  note right of Extraction
    A struct, NOT a typestate.
    A node can extract fine AND carry a
    complaint of its own — an unknown key
    is the PARENT failing to consume its
    input while the value stays good.
    Two states could not say that.
    (#cleanup)
  end note

  class "Extracted<T, I>" as Extracted {
    -extraction: Extraction<T>
    -source: I
    --
    +new(Extraction<T>, I) -> Self
    +source() -> &I
    +extraction() -> &Extraction<T>
    +into_extraction() -> Extraction<T>
    +value() -> Option<&T>
    +reasons() -> &[Reason]
    +to_error(msg) -> syn::Error
  }
  note right of Extracted
    The extractor's OUTPUT and the
    processor's INPUT. Source lives here,
    not behind ""T: Sourced"", because a
    FAILED extraction has no T to ask —
    which is the case a diagnostic needs
    most. (#extracted/source-when-absent)

    ""new"" is public and must be: the
    stage impls live in the other crate.
    Not a capability token.
  end note

  class Reason {
    +kind: ReasonKind
    -span: Option<Span>
    --
    +new(ReasonKind) -> Self
    +at(ReasonKind, &impl Spanned) -> Self
    +span() -> Option<Span>
    +to_error(&impl ToTokens, msg) -> syn::Error
  }
  note left of Reason
    Stores a **Span**, while ""Extracted""
    stores a **node**. Deliberate asymmetry:
    a node is multi-token, so ""new_spanned""
    is needed for its full range; a reason
    points at ONE token, which needs no
    ""Span::join"" and is therefore exact.

    ""to_error"" takes the fallback node as an
    ARGUMENT — position belongs to where a
    reason sits in the tree, not to the
    reason. (#reason/span-not-node)
  end note

  enum ReasonKind {
    WrongShape
    UnknownKey
    Missing
    Duplicate
    Ambiguous
    Custom(String)
  }
  note bottom of ReasonKind
    CLOSED reasons, open rendering.
    Closed so the framework can interpret
    what it caught; ""Custom"" so an exotic
    grammar is never blocked outright.
  end note

  interface "Sourced<'ast>" as Sourced {
    +type Source: ToTokens
    +source() -> &'ast Source
    +additional() -> &[&'ast Source]
  }
}

package proc_macro_flow_derive <<Frame>> {

  interface "Extractor<'ast, I>" as Extractor {
    +type Output
    +extract_from(I) -> Self::Output
  }
  note right of Extractor
    Supertraits are the two questions:
    ""Sourced"" = what is the source,
    ""I: Visitable"" = how do we get there.
    No third question about PARSING.

    ""Output"" is unbounded on purpose until
    Processor exists (#extractor/output-bound).
  end note

  interface "Validate<'ast, I>" as Validate {
    +type ValidityError
    +type Valid
    +validate(I) -> Result<Valid, ValidityError>
  }
  note bottom of Validate
    SURFACE-LEVEL ONLY: does this exist
    where required, is this within a bound.
    Never parsing, never grammar.
    (#pipeline/validity-scope)
  end note

  interface "Visitable<'ast>" as Visitable {
    +accept<V: Visit<'ast>>(self, &mut V)
  }
  note bottom of Visitable
    Implemented for the REFERENCE types
    (""&'ast syn::Attribute""), so ""self"" is
    already the ""&'ast T"" every ""visit_*""
    wants. Implementing it for the owned
    type made the receiver unconstructible
    for value-passed wrappers.
    (#visitable/by-value)
  end note

  ' --- free functions: what #[from] lowers to ---
  class "extract / extract_each / extract_maybe" as FromHelpers <<(F,#FFCC88)>> {
    extract<T, I>(I) -> T::Output
    extract_each<T, I, N>(N) -> Vec<T::Output>
    extract_maybe<T, I>(Option<I>) -> Option<T::Output>
  }
  note bottom of FromHelpers
    The lowering target of ""#[from = ..]"".
    Which one a field uses is read off its
    TYPE, never off the attribute
    (#from/arity-from-type).

    Call sites must name T: ""T::Output"" is
    an associated type and so not
    injective (#from/names-its-target).
  end note
}

Extracted *-- Extraction
Extraction *-- "0..*" Reason
Reason *-- ReasonKind
Extractor --|> Sourced
Extractor --|> Validate
Extractor ..> Extracted : Output is\ntypically
FromHelpers ..> Extractor : drives

@enduml
